.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1034 AM PDT Mon Oct 19 2026

Currently MVFR-VFR. Stratus is dissipating with VFR expected by the
afternoon. High clouds are streaming in from the southwest and will
increase in coverage through the TAF period. Onshore winds this
morning and this afternoon will back through the TAF period to
become southerly. While there`s no precipitation in the TAFs, there
is a chance for rain showers Tuesday, especially across the coastal
waters. The incoming low pressure system will deepen and mix out the
marine layer, likely keeping the terminals VFR after this morning.

Vicinity of SFO...Currently MVFR with westerly flow. High confidence
in VFR prevailing by this afternoon. Westerly winds will diminish
and begin to back this evening, becoming southeasterly overnight and
northwesterly tomorrow afternoon.

SFO Bridge Approach...After this morning, the San Mateo Bridge
Approach will likely remain clear of clouds below FL070.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Currently MVFR with westerly flow at MRY
and MVFR with southerly flow at SNS. High confidence in VFR
prevailing by this afternoon. Westerly winds will diminish and begin
to back this evening, becoming southeasterly overnight.

